{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408929-fun-with-firedust-and-other-unstable-concoctions","id":1408929,"title":"Fun With Firedust (and other unstable concoctions)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-18T07:51:17-07:00","id":1408929,"title":"Fun With Firedust (and other unstable concoctions)","content":"I'm bringing my West game back to life and one of my players has an awesome idea for a witch doctor Twilight that uses a mixture of Thaumaturgy and Sorcery to concoct strange and likely dangerous alchemical mixtures and ideally throw them at people. As far as I know Firedust grenades haven't made it over to 3E officially yet, but has anyone made some solid fan content or have ideas on how they'd work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T08:38:11-07:00","id":1408935,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve thought about this a lot, and the answer is really complex. Basically explosives or other AoE attacks are a bit weird in ex3. If they\u2019re withering you usually get only the highest initiative damage, plus one for each other hit target, and for decisive you have to divvy up your initiative between hit targets to do damage.<br /> <br /> BUT all of the charms that let you do that, I think universally, are Simple and cost notes and willpower. So basically, you can\u2019t use them as just a weapon, because if you do somebody could combo that AoE weapon with other Simple charms, especially multiple attack charms, and be insanely overpowered for the cost you pay. The only way I found to balance them out properly is to make it a gambit that, if successful, creates a one time environmental hazard. Also explicitly it is not compatible with any multiple attack charms or anything unless they specify that they work with grenades, just in case some charm out there would let you do multiple gambits at once. <br /> <br /> For guidelines I\u2019d say make the gambit difficulty 5 and it creates a bonfire hazard to everything within Close range of the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T08:45:49-07:00","id":1408939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408929-fun-with-firedust-and-other-unstable-concoctions?p=1408935#post1408935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve thought about this a lot, and the answer is really complex. Basically explosives or other AoE attacks are a bit weird in ex3. If they\u2019re withering you usually get only the highest initiative damage, plus one for each other hit target, and for decisive you have to divvy up your initiative between hit targets to do damage.<br /> <br /> BUT all of the charms that let you do that, I think universally, are Simple and cost notes and willpower. So basically, you can\u2019t use them as just a weapon, because if you do somebody could combo that AoE weapon with other Simple charms, especially multiple attack charms, and be insanely overpowered for the cost you pay. The only way I found to balance them out properly is to make it a gambit that, if successful, creates a one time environmental hazard. Also explicitly it is not compatible with any multiple attack charms or anything unless they specify that they work with grenades, just in case some charm out there would let you do multiple gambits at once. <br /> <br /> For guidelines I\u2019d say make the gambit difficulty 5 and it creates a bonfire hazard to everything within Close range of the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo, that's a really clever way of doing it. Combined with just a, I dunno, medium thrown weapon statline you can get up to some shenanigans with that and would also play nice with some of the other stuff the players is interested in doing. (To quote, &quot;Would Cascade of Cutting Terror mean i can carpet bomb?&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T10:19:35-07:00","id":1408968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408929-fun-with-firedust-and-other-unstable-concoctions?p=1408935#post1408935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For guidelines I\u2019d say make the gambit difficulty 5 and it creates a bonfire hazard to everything within Close range of the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree about using gambits for this, but I think difficulty 5 is probably a bit too high. That's usually going to require something like 12 initiative to pull off, and should be roughly equivalent in effectiveness to doing 5 lethal damage. I don't think the environmental hazard caused by a firedust grenade is that potent. Even if you use bonfire stats, that's still only doing 4L/round, meaning an absolute maximum of 4 lethal damage if every die rolls a success. And, of course, difficulty 5 means that mortal soldiers will rarely be pulling this off. On the whole, I'd prefer a difficulty of 3.<br /> <br /> If you do keep the difficulty of 5, though, I'd suggest that if you fail to meet the difficulty, the hazard still goes off, it just goes off at the end of the turn, instead of on the moment the attack is made. If anyone in the area has a reflexive move left, they can use it to move out of the area. That gives some benefit to firedust grenade throwing even if you can't meet the difficulty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T10:36:35-07:00","id":1408971,"title":"","content":"What about difficulty 4, but it also applies an onslaught penalty to everyone, even if they weren\u2019t the original target?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T11:59:28-07:00","id":1408980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408929-fun-with-firedust-and-other-unstable-concoctions?p=1408971#post1408971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about difficulty 4, but it also applies an onslaught penalty to everyone, even if they weren\u2019t the original target?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally, if it's going to be an environmental hazard, I'd prefer if it was treated that way - no other environmental hazard imposes an onslaught penalty for getting out of it. At most, I think the specific person targeted by the gambit should take an onslaught penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T00:04:28-07:00","id":1409084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408929-fun-with-firedust-and-other-unstable-concoctions?p=1408939#post1408939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooo, that's a really clever way of doing it. Combined with just a, I dunno, medium thrown weapon statline you can get up to some shenanigans with that and would also play nice with some of the other stuff the players is interested in doing. (To quote, &quot;Would Cascade of Cutting Terror mean i can carpet bomb?&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd slap the Subtle tag on it, too, so that it can <i>only</i> be used for these gambits (and disarming, unhorsing, and so on, which could be fun to stunt).<br /> <br /> Subtle tag or no, if you have <b>Miracles of the Solar Exalted</b>, show your player the Charms <i>Spitting Hand Discipline</i> and <i>Death-Dealing Diffusion</i>.<br /> <br /> EDIT: One of the <b>Adversaries of the Righteous</b> entries (the Quaghead Tribe) includes a gambit for blowing things up with a firewand or burning arrow. It's Difficulty 4 to create a 4L hazard out to short range (Difficulty 5 to resist), which should give you a ballpark for how to balance these concoctions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 08-19-2020, 03:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T16:20:29-07:00","id":1409247,"title":"","content":"According to that same entry it\u2019s only a difficulty 1 gambit to poison someone by throwing a live snake at them. Just something people should know. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T06:56:53-07:00","id":1409341,"title":"","content":"I'm increasingly leaning more towards mundane grenades being a Thrown weapon with the same stats as a Flamepiece or Firewand (depending on the payload) rather than trying to model the splash as an environmental hazard. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T07:31:43-07:00","id":1409349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408929-fun-with-firedust-and-other-unstable-concoctions?p=1409341#post1409341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm increasingly leaning more towards mundane grenades being a Thrown weapon with the same stats as a Flamepiece or Firewand (depending on the payload) rather than trying to model the splash as an environmental hazard. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My current plan for my game is now a hybrid of the two (since the player is specifically wanted to do insane alchemical things like piss of a Storm Mother enough that she strikes them with lightning then use sorcery/thaumaturgy to capture and bottle it)<br /> <br /> For general purpose &quot;throwing something at someone to hurt them&quot; it'll be a thrown weapon tagged like a firewand, with size depending on payload and stuff. Then allow the Gambit (probably dif 4, though I might just average the difficulties of environmental hazards) with the restrictions DrLovemonkey listed for fun battlefield control. Because the player is insanely creative, i love their kind of crazy, and they want to do things like piss off Storm Mothers, Storm Serpents, and gods know what else in a game set in the west.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T07:48:41-07:00","id":1409352,"title":"","content":"Here's version 1.0 so far.<br /> Bottled Fury<br /> Tags: Lethal, Thrown (Short), Flame, Hazardous<br /> <br /> Hazardous: This weapon can make hazardous attacks. Hazardous attacks sacrifice one Defense until the character\u2019s next turn. The wielder can than make a hazard gambit (diff 4). If successful the target of the gambit suffers damage as per a regular decisive attack and all creatures within close range of the target are subject to a environmental hazard determined by the contents of bottle. This hazard lasts a single turn unless supported by external circumstances (Fire in a dry field, mud in a corridor, etc). This gambit is incompatible with multi-attack charms or other effects unless they explicitly effect grenades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":882,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","user":"SamuraiMujuru","date":". 08-20-2020, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T09:04:55-07:00","id":1409366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408929-fun-with-firedust-and-other-unstable-concoctions?p=1409349#post1409349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My current plan for my game is now a hybrid of the two (since the player is specifically wanted to do insane alchemical things like piss of a Storm Mother enough that she strikes them with lightning then use sorcery/thaumaturgy to capture and bottle it)</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, it'll help a lot if the player's actively making their own concoctions. \u200bThe main thing you want to avoid is one player having battlefield control for virtually every action in every combat just because of the molotov cocktails they're tossing around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T09:49:16-07:00","id":1409372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408929-fun-with-firedust-and-other-unstable-concoctions?p=1409366#post1409366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, it'll help a lot if the player's actively making their own concoctions. \u200bThe main thing you want to avoid is one player having battlefield control for virtually every action in every combat just because of the molotov cocktails they're tossing around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. With a gambit at difficulty 4 a user can't spam 3i decisives over and over.<br /> <br /> Further discussion in my group led to just trying to trigger the hazard without specifically targeting anyone. My current theoretical solution is the &quot;defense&quot; you're targeting is the difficulty of the hazard itself and there's no target for the actual Decisive attack portion, with failure meaning you drop it on yourself. Which then led to a very silly discussion of bottling and throwing a fragment of the silent wind and really hoping you don't drop that on yourself.<br /> <br /> For cool narrative things like knocking over a bookshelf in a chase planning on resolving it like a regular old hazard, you just have an easy way to trigger them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":882,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","user":"SamuraiMujuru","date":". 08-20-2020, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T21:07:43-07:00","id":1409460,"title":"","content":"An alternate approach for grenades is to abstract their splash effect out into something that makes them more effective against battle groups. Not sure what would be balanced for that though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}